# Contract: Specification Catalog (CATALOG.md)

**Location**: `.github/specs/CATALOG.md`
**Purpose**: Centralized, discoverable index of all specifications
**Consumers**: Governance team, stakeholders, specification maintainers
**Version**: 1.0

## Interface Specification

### File Format & Structure

**Format**: GitHub Markdown (CommonMark)

**Required Sections**:

```markdown
# Specification Catalog

## Overview
Brief statement of purpose (2-3 sentences)

## Catalog Schema (Canonical)

**Table Structure**: `| # | Slug | Title | Status | Created | Link |`

This canonical schema is used for all specification index tables (Active, Draft, Archived).

## Active Specifications

| # | Slug | Title | Status | Created | Link |
|---|------|-------|--------|---------|------|
| [number] | [slug] | [title] | [status] | [date] | [link] |
| ... |

## Draft Specifications

| # | Slug | Title | Status | Created | Link |
|---|------|-------|--------|---------|------|
| [number] | [slug] | [title] | [status] | [date] | [link] |
| ... |

## Detailed Entries

### [NNN] - [Title]
[Specification summary: 2-3 sentences]
- **Status**: [Draft/Active/Archived]
- **Phase**: [Draft/Clarified/Planned/TasksGenerated/InProgress/Complete]
- **Created**: [YYYY-MM-DD]
- **Updated**: [YYYY-MM-DD]
- **Link**: [./NNN-slug/spec.md](./NNN-slug/spec.md)

### [NNN+1] - [Title]
[Additional specs follow same pattern]

## Archive

Archived/deprecated specifications (if any)
```

### Content Rules

**Canonical Index Table Schema**:

- Format: `| # | Slug | Title | Status | Created | Link |` (exactly 6 columns in this order)
- Used for all status-based tables: Active Specifications, Draft Specifications, Archived Specifications
- One row per specification (001, 002, ..., 013+)
- Sorted by specification number (ascending)

**Column Definitions**:

- `#` column: 3-digit number (left-padded with zeros)
- `Slug` column: Directory slug derived from directory name (e.g., "spec-folder-refactor" from "013-spec-folder-refactor")
- `Title` column: Full specification title
- `Status` column: One of `Draft`, `Active`, `Archived` (canonical enum)
- `Created` column: ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD)
- `Link` column: Markdown link to `./NNN-{slug}/spec.md`

**Detailed Entries**:

- One detailed entry per specification (same order as table)
- Heading format: `### NNN - Title` (3-digit number + dash + title)
- Summary: 2-3 plain-language sentences
- Metadata fields: Status, Phase, Created, Updated, Link
- Link must be relative (`./{number}-{slug}/spec.md`)

### Data Freshness Requirements

- **Link Validity**: All links must point to existing specification directories
- **Status Accuracy**: Specification status in CATALOG.md must match Specification.status in spec.md
- **Date Accuracy**: Created/Updated dates must be accurate to ±7 days
- **Completeness**: 100% of specifications in `.github/specs/` must appear in CATALOG.md
- **Update Frequency**: CATALOG.md must be updated within 7 days of any new specification creation (SC-008)

### Usage Scenarios

**User Story 1 - Discovery**: Governance team opens CATALOG.md and sees all 12+ specifications at a glance

- ✅ Can scan index table to find desired specification
- ✅ Can identify specification by number, title, or status
- ✅ Can navigate to detailed entry for more information

**User Story 2 - Navigation**: Team member needs to locate a specific specification

- ✅ Uses Ctrl+F or browser search to find keyword/number
- ✅ Locates detailed entry and clicks link
- ✅ Navigates to specification directory in <30 seconds (SC-007)

**User Story 3 - Status Tracking**: Manager wants to see which specs are in progress, complete, or draft

- ✅ Scans Status column in index table
- ✅ Identifies complete vs. active vs. draft specifications
- ✅ Understands overall governance progress

**User Story 4 - New Contributor Onboarding**: New team member wants to understand governance specifications

- ✅ Opens CATALOG.md as entry point to governance system
- ✅ Reads overview and discovers all active specifications
- ✅ Picks a specification to read and understand structure

---

## Acceptance Criteria

- ✅ CATALOG.md exists at `.github/specs/CATALOG.md`
- ✅ All 12+ specifications appear in catalog with accurate metadata
- ✅ All links are valid and point to correct spec directories
- ✅ Catalog is linked from CLAUDE.md with clear navigation instructions
- ✅ User can locate any specification in <30 seconds using catalog (SC-007)
- ✅ Catalog is updated within 7 days of new specification creation (SC-008)

---

